        },
        {
          "comment": "Featured story: Lab Submission Format",
          "raw_html": "      <div style=\"display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px; align-items: flex-start; margin: 0 0 24px 0;\">\n        <div style=\"flex: 0 0 25%; min-width: 280px;\">\n          <a href=\"https://jfnewsom.github.io/is2053-assets/pages/support/submission-format.html\"\n             aria-label=\"Open the Lab Submission Format reference page\">\n            <img src=\"https://jfnewsom.github.io/is2053-assets/pages/support/images/lab-submission-format.png\"\n                 alt=\"Lab submission format reference: an annotated example of lab-1-1.py\"\n                 style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; border: 1px solid #464646;\">\n          </a>\n        </div>\n        <div style=\"flex: 1 1 320px;\">\n          <div class=\"lc-h3 lc-h3--green\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">New Reference: Lab Submission Format</div>\n          <p>Every <code>lab-X-Y.py</code> file you submit to CodeGrade follows the same structure: a docstring header at the top, named constants, <code>def main():</code> with 4-space indentation, inline comments before each block, and the standard <code>if __name__ == '__main__':</code> entry point at the bottom.</p>\n          <p>Getting the format right is worth up to <strong>23 points per lab</strong> across the Documentation and Code Style rubric categories. This visual reference shows you exactly what a clean submission looks like, with rules color-coded by category.</p>\n          <a href=\"https://jfnewsom.github.io/is2053-assets/pages/support/submission-format.html\" class=\"lc-cta-btn\" style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n            Open the format reference &rarr;\n          </a>\n        </div>\n      </div>"
        },
        {
          "comment": "Welcome video. PER MODALITY, not online-only (F-027): 904 gets its own recording rather than a blank space.",
          "modality": "onl",
          "raw_html": "      <div style=\"display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px; align-items: flex-start; margin: 0 0 24px 0;\">\n        <div style=\"flex: 0 0 25%; min-width: 280px;\">\n          <div style=\"position: relative; width: 100%; height: 0; padding-bottom: 56.25%;\">\n            <iframe src=\"https://utsa.hosted.panopto.com/Panopto/Pages/Embed.aspx?id=86b634f7-a7eb-4b80-b921-b482011520a3&autoplay=false&offerviewer=true&showtitle=true&showbrand=false&captions=false&interactivity=all\"\n                    style=\"border: 1px solid #464646; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"\n                    allowfullscreen allow=\"autoplay\"\n                    aria-label=\"Panopto Embedded Video Player\"\n                    aria-description=\"IS2053 Fall Welcome\"></iframe>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div style=\"flex: 1 1 320px;\">\n          <div class=\"lc-h3 lc-h3--yellow\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Welcome Video</div>\n          <p>In this short welcome video I introduce myself, walk you through how this course works, and frame what you&rsquo;re signing up for. I cover the &ldquo;pain before magic&rdquo; teaching philosophy, where sometimes you&rsquo;ll solve a problem with clunky tools so that the right tool, when it arrives, actually sticks, and I lay out the five-module arc that takes you from <strong>variables and decisions</strong> through loops, functions, files, and dictionaries, all the way to <strong>classes and objects</strong> (Python chapters 2 through 10).</p>\n          <p>You&rsquo;ll learn that in this course you aren&rsquo;t a student, you&rsquo;re a <strong>Junior Developer at Bat City Collective</strong>, an Austin indie game studio building a retro Texas road trip game called <em>Deep in the Heart: A Lone Star Journey</em> for our client, All My Eggses Live in Texas. I introduce the five mentor voices you&rsquo;ll hear all semester (Danny, Priya, Sasha, T-Bone, and Tyler) and explain the <strong>BUILD &rarr; ENHANCE &rarr; MASTER</strong> rhythm where each module&rsquo;s three labs build on the same growing codebase.</p>\n          <p>I also walk through the logistics: every lab is auto-graded by <strong>CodeGrade</strong> with the same five-category rubric for everyone, <strong>Discord</strong> is the first stop for questions and email is for anything personal or FERPA-sensitive, our <strong>Tuesday 6 PM Central office hours</strong> are drop-in Q&amp;A for both my classes, and there&rsquo;s no late work but the lowest grade in each category drops automatically. AI is allowed for explanations and debugging, not for generating code you submit, and you should be ready to defend any line you turn in.</p>\n          <p>The video closes with your <strong>first 72 hours</strong>: install Python and VS Code, read the syllabus and the Lab 1.1 assignment sheet, join Discord using the invite link on the <strong>Discord</strong> page in the left navigation, and get your first BookEx and Lab 1.1 submitted by the end of the first week.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>"
        },
        {
          "comment": "Face-to-face welcome video. Instructions are inside the block. check_pending.py owns the deadline and nags until it lands.",
          "modality": "f2f",
          "raw_html": "      <!-- F2F_WELCOME_VIDEO_PENDING\n           TO PUBLISH THE 904 WELCOME VIDEO:\n             1. Replace PANOPTO_ID_904_PENDING below with the Panopto id.\n             2. Delete the first line of this block, and delete the final line,\n                which is the one that closes this comment. Nothing else.\n                Do NOT add F2F_ONLY sentinel comments. The renderer emits those\n                from this block's \"modality\": \"f2f\" key, and adding them by hand\n                would fence the block twice.\n             3. ./render_all.sh  then push. check_pending.py stops nagging.\n           The synopsis below is a placeholder. Write it in your own voice, or\n           delete the div that holds it if 904 does not need one.\n      <div style=\"display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px; align-items: flex-start; margin: 0 0 24px 0;\">\n        <div style=\"flex: 0 0 25%; min-width: 280px;\">\n          <div style=\"position: relative; width: 100%; height: 0; padding-bottom: 56.25%;\">\n            <iframe src=\"https://utsa.hosted.panopto.com/Panopto/Pages/Embed.aspx?id=PANOPTO_ID_904_PENDING&autoplay=false&offerviewer=true&showtitle=true&showbrand=false&captions=false&interactivity=all\"\n                    style=\"border: 1px solid #464646; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"\n                    allowfullscreen allow=\"autoplay\"\n                    aria-label=\"Panopto Embedded Video Player\"\n                    aria-description=\"IS2053 Fall Welcome, Section 904\"></iframe>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div style=\"flex: 1 1 320px;\">\n          <div class=\"lc-h3 lc-h3--yellow\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Welcome Video</div>\n          <p>PLACEHOLDER SYNOPSIS. Write what this video covers for 904.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      -->"
        },
        {
          "comment": "Bat City narrative intro",
          "raw_html": "      <div class=\"lc-narrative-intro\">\n        <div class=\"lc-narrative-intro__body\">\n          <div class=\"lc-narrative-intro__tagline\">This course is structured as a semester-long game development engagement.</div>\n          <p>\n            You&rsquo;re a <strong>Junior Developer</strong> at <strong>Bat City Collective</strong>, an\n            Austin indie game studio. Over five modules you&rsquo;ll build a retro text adventure called\n            <em>Deep in the Heart: A Lone Star Journey</em> for your client, the Texas-themed\n            restaurant chain <strong>All My Eggses Live in Texas</strong>. Every module is a sprint:\n            BUILD a feature, ENHANCE it, then MASTER it.\n          </p>\n          <p>\n            This isn&rsquo;t homework. It&rsquo;s a product. The game has a real brief, real constraints,\n            real stakeholders, and a real shipping deadline at the end of the term. The Python concepts\n            you learn, from variables and loops through functions, files, and classes, all serve the game.\n            Learn more about <a href=\"https://jfnewsom.github.io/is2053-assets/pages/scenario/scenario.html\">the scenario</a>,\n            <a href=\"https://jfnewsom.github.io/is2053-assets/pages/scenario/bat-city.html\">Bat City Collective</a>,\n            or <a href=\"https://jfnewsom.github.io/is2053-assets/pages/scenario/all-my-eggses.html\">your client</a>.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n        <img class=\"lc-narrative-intro__logo\"\n             src=\"https://jfnewsom.github.io/is2053-assets/branding/AllMyEggses3D-Full.png\"\n             alt=\"All My Eggses Live in Texas\">\n      </div>"
        },
        {
          "comment": "2-card client/studio grid",
          "label": "The Engagement",
          "body_html": "      <div class=\"lc-client-grid\">\n        <div class=\"lc-client-card\" style=\"--client-color: var(--bat-yellow);\">\n          <div class=\"lc-client-card__role\">Your Studio</div>\n          <div class=\"lc-client-card__name\">Bat City Collective</div>\n          <p class=\"lc-client-card__body\">\n            Austin indie game studio specializing in retro-style games and text adventures. Founded\n            by devs burned out by AAA crunch culture. Five mentors will guide you across the\n            project: Danny (Lead Dev), Priya (PM), Sasha (Creative), T-Bone (QA), and Tyler (Junior\n            Dev, your peer).\n          </p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"lc-client-card\" style=\"--client-color: var(--neon-orange);\">\n          <div class=\"lc-client-card__role\">Your Client</div>\n          <div class=\"lc-client-card__name\">All My Eggses Live in Texas</div>\n          <p class=\"lc-client-card__body\">\n            Texas-themed family restaurant chain (think Cracker Barrel meets Buc-ee&rsquo;s).\n            47 locations. They want a retro game for the tablets that are replacing the peg games\n            on every table. The brief: <em>&ldquo;Oregon Trail but TEXAS. Family-friendly. 5&ndash;10\n            minutes. No violence.&rdquo;</em>\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      </div>"
